 "result_text": "`generate_uid()` now always returns a 64-character UID when you don't pass `entropy_srcs`. That should stop the intermittent `test_add_dataset` failure, since that test depends on the UID length. I haven't run the test suite. As a quick check, 20,000 generated UIDs all came out at exactly 64 characters.\n\nYour guess about the UID lengths was right. The suffix was a random number below `10**(64 - len(prefix))`, so it was sometimes shorter than the maximum. The UID, and so the encoded dataset, then varied by a few bytes. That is what moved the offset from 398 to 396.\n\nThe fix is in `src/pydicom/uid.py`. The suffix is now drawn so that it always has exactly `64 - len(prefix)` digits and never starts with a zero, which also keeps it a valid UID component.\n\nI didn't look into `test_encoders.py::TestDatasetCompress::test_round_trip`. That one is a separate problem from the UID length, and your memory-reuse guess is still open.",
